{"duration_api_ms":5334,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"00398537-58fc-462f-9125-0a660be28f52","total_cost_usd":0.0010246,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1066,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1277,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":931},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1066,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1277,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1066},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1609,"outputTokens":1301,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1066,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0010246,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":931,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":1066,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Why ETFs can distribute fewer gains:** When an authorized participant redeems ETF shares, the fund can deliver low-basis securities in kind rather than selling them for cash. Under IRC §852(b)(6), a RIC recognizes no gain on that in-kind distribution, so it can purge its most appreciated lots without realizing gains. A cash-redeeming mutual fund must sell holdings, and those sales can generate capital gain distributions passed to all remaining shareholders.\n\n**Limits:**\n- The benefit applies only to in-kind redemptions. Cash creations and redemptions and rebalancing or index-change sales can still realize gains.\n- It depends on AP participation. Many bond and international ETFs rely more on cash.\n- Short-term gains still distribute as ordinary income. Dividends and interest are unaffected.\n- Your own sale of ETF shares is still taxable. The benefit avoids fund-level distributions, not tax altogether.\n- It requires RIC qualification, and the result is deferral, not permanent exemption.","ttft_ms":3583,"type":"result","duration_ms":4590,"uuid":"94df6044-11a6-4a01-8b1e-462a53770e5c","ttft_stream_ms":398,"time_to_request_ms":48,"first_content_frame_ms":398,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
